{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",

  // Cloudflare Pages project config.
  //
  // `pages_build_output_dir` is what marks this as a Pages project rather than
  // a Worker — there is deliberately no `main` entrypoint, because the site is
  // pure static output with no server-side code. If a `main` key ever appears
  // here, something has gone wrong: this project's Pages project has no
  // backend of its own by design (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md). That warning stays
  // scoped to THIS file — `workers/flight-sightings-cron/wrangler.jsonc` is a
  // separate, standalone Worker deployable with its own `main`, deployed
  // independently of this Pages project specifically because it needs a Cron
  // Trigger, which Pages Functions cannot have.
  //
  // The narrow exceptions here are `functions/api/` routes: ice-flights.js
  // and trace/[hex].js — Cloudflare Pages Functions (not a Worker `main`, and
  // need none of the config below to run). They exist only because adsb.lol
  // sends no CORS headers, so something server-side has to relay its
  // response; they hold no state, no binding, and nothing written anywhere.
  // See "Live flight proxy" in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md for the full rationale and
  // what they deliberately do not do. `functions/api/flight-log/*` is the
  // second exception — read-only D1 access, see the binding comment below.
  //
  // Deployment is via Pages' Git integration, so Cloudflare runs the build
  // itself. That is chosen over a deploy workflow specifically because it
  // builds a preview URL for every pull request — for a project asking for
  // community contributions, a reviewer clicking a working link beats asking a
  // first-time contributor to set up Node locally.
  //
  // Build settings to set in the dashboard (or accept from framework detection):
  //   Build command:        npm run build
  //   Build output dir:     dist
  //   Node version:         22  (see "engines" in package.json)

  // The Cloudflare Pages project, which is the Minnesota deployment of FlockOff
  // and carries the state in its name. The project is FlockOff; this is where
  // this instance of it is served from, and the two are not the same string.
  "name": "flockoffmn",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./dist",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-07-30",

  // One binding, narrowly scoped: FLIGHT_SIGHTINGS_DB, a Cloudflare D1
  // database. It is read-only in application code — it backs
  // functions/api/flight-log/{index,[hex],export}.js and
  // functions/flight-log/record/{[id],[id]/pdf}.js, all SELECT-only, never
  // INSERT/UPDATE. It holds aircraft-level facts (hex, callsign,
  // ground-arrival/departure timestamps — see
  // migrations/0001_flight_sightings.sql) and nothing about a visitor: no
  // query is logged, no IP or request identifier is stored anywhere.
  //
  // The write path lives entirely in the separate, standalone
  // workers/flight-sightings-cron/ deployable (its own wrangler.jsonc, its
  // own D1 binding, its own Cron Trigger) — NOT in this Pages project. See
  // that Worker's index.mjs header and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md's "Flight
  // sighting log (the second exception)" section for the full rationale.
  //
  // Still no KV, no queues, no secrets here, and no R2 *binding* — the
  // self-hosted basemap (see "Base map tiles" below) lives in a separate,
  // unbound `flockoffmn-tiles` R2 bucket that this Pages project never
  // reads from and this file never references. The browser talks to that
  // bucket's public URL directly (a static file, requested by byte range),
  // the same shape as MapTiler before it, just self-hosted. Nothing here
  // gains a way to read or write it. Adding an actual binding — one this
  // application code touches — is still the thing to think twice about:
  // it means adding another place data could accumulate, and that still
  // shouldn't happen without revisiting the privacy claims on /about and
  // this file's own reasoning.
  //
  // This top-level copy is inherited by nothing deployed — see the `env`
  // block below: declaring env.preview/env.production at all makes bindings
  // non-inheritable, so both keep their own identical copy. This one only
  // matters for `wrangler pages dev` and a manual `wrangler pages deploy`.
  // Rotating database_id means editing three places, not one; there's no
  // build-time check that they stay in sync.
  "d1_databases": [
    {
      "binding": "FLIGHT_SIGHTINGS_DB",
      "database_name": "flockoffmn-flight-sightings",
      "database_id": "90f43a8b-be4e-437c-ae31-097f1fc88a2b"
    }
  ],

  // Base map tiles. This used to be a MapTiler API key (see git history —
  // docs/DEPLOYMENT.md's old "MapTiler quick start" section had ~80 lines
  // about origin restriction and a Pages-secrets-vs-build-time-vars trap
  // that shipped a broken basemap to production twice). That's gone: the
  // basemap is now one self-hosted PMTiles archive, built once from OSM data
  // by scripts/tiles/build-basemap.mjs and served from a public,
  // *unbound* R2 bucket (see the d1_databases comment above for why unbound
  // matters). No vendor, no key, no request-count ceiling, no origin
  // restriction to verify.
  //
  // PUBLIC_TILES_URL is optional — mapStyle.ts already defaults to the real
  // production archive's URL, so this repo works with zero env config out of
  // the box (`npm run dev` points at the same public bucket production
  // does — see that file's header comment for why that's the right
  // tradeoff for a newcomer's first `npm run dev`). Set it only if you're
  // running your own fork against your own bucket; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
  // § Base map tiles for the rebuild-and-upload runbook.
  "vars": {},
  "env": {
    // Declaring `env` at all makes every binding non-inheritable, including
    // ones this section doesn't mention — Cloudflare stops falling back to
    // the top-level `d1_databases` the moment `env.preview` exists, even
    // though preview always had that binding before this file had an `env`
    // block. Confirmed live: earlier PR previews (#46, #48) served
    // /api/flight-log/ fine; a preview built from a first draft of this
    // change that omitted d1_databases here returned a 500 ("Cannot read
    // properties of undefined (reading 'prepare')"). Keep this in sync with
    // the top-level and env.production copies below — see that block's
    // comment for what the binding is for.
    "preview": {
      "d1_databases": [
        {
          "binding": "FLIGHT_SIGHTINGS_DB",
          "database_name": "flockoffmn-flight-sightings",
          "database_id": "90f43a8b-be4e-437c-ae31-097f1fc88a2b"
        }
      ],
      // Same public bucket as production — a preview deploy and the live
      // site read the same static archive (it carries no visitor data, so
      // there's no separation concern the way there would be for the D1
      // binding above). Explicit here rather than left to mapStyle.ts's
      // built-in default so a future bucket-URL change is a one-line edit
      // in the file that already documents it, not an app-code change.
      "vars": {
        "PUBLIC_TILES_URL": "https://tiles.flockoffmn.org/minnesota.pmtiles"
      }
    },
    "production": {
      "d1_databases": [
        {
          "binding": "FLIGHT_SIGHTINGS_DB",
          "database_name": "flockoffmn-flight-sightings",
          "database_id": "90f43a8b-be4e-437c-ae31-097f1fc88a2b"
        }
      ],
      "vars": {
        "PUBLIC_TILES_URL": "https://tiles.flockoffmn.org/minnesota.pmtiles"
      }
    }
  }
}
